{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition","id":1356470,"title":"CHALLENGE! Build the Hulk in Aberrant 1st Edition & 2nd (Beta) Edition!!!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-22T06:04:40-08:00","id":1356470,"title":"CHALLENGE! Build the Hulk in Aberrant 1st Edition & 2nd (Beta) Edition!!!","content":"I am curious how the two additions differ in bringing PC concepts to life. I would like to see how others can use Marvel's Incredible Hulk as a base 'concept' to show the PC creation system's in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T08:46:10-08:00","id":1356485,"title":"","content":"Quick question before even try, but, how much experience is allowed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T11:29:57-08:00","id":1356506,"title":"","content":"One issue with the hulk in 2E is that the easiest way to model him is to take a bunch of transcendents given that some of the high level taints are pretty much what makes the Hulk (the rage trigger), but there's no way, IMO to emulate what happened in the MCU where banner got in touch with his inner hulk and got control, so you'd need a house rule to allow for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T12:22:06-08:00","id":1356513,"title":"","content":"For 2E, I'd probably go with Transformation 5, which requires Quantum 4. Give the power a 1-point tag to drop Dr. Banner's Intellect, Presence, and Manipulation to 1, while raising his Might and Stamina to 5. Give him a -1 tag to make the change based on getting angry/calm. Give it a -1?/-2? tag to limit him to a single alternate form (he can Max Out to briefly overcome the limitation and become a variant Hulk). Add a +1 or +2 Duration tag to make the power last minutes or hours. Finish by giving the power the +1 Extra Traits tag as many times as you have XP to spare. The base power will give him 5 dots from a laundry list of Hulk-appropriate traits, and each purchase of the Extra Traits tag will give him 5 more. Taking the tag the max of 5 times gives him 30 dots to spread around his Hulk form, which should be plenty.<br /> <br /> He'll likely need Mega-Might and Mega-Stamina 5, as well as a few levels of Durability. Most of the Might based Mega-Edges would be appropriate as well, as are a good chunk of the Stamina Mega-Edges. The Hulk is technically highly acrobatic, but this never seems to come up, so just give him Mega-Dexterity 1. He has super keen senses (he can perceive astral forms), so add on a sensory Mega-Edge. I don't think he actually needs to take the Growth power, since Transformation presumably covers him becoming really big.<br /> <br /> Raising Quantum to 4 should be 48 points.<br /> Transformation 5 would be 60 points.<br /> Five Extra Trait tags cost 60 points.<br /> Assume the single form limitation and Duration enhancement tags cancel out.<br /> Swapping mental/social stats for physical and limiting the change to an anger trigger cancel out.<br /> End total is 168 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 12-22-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:11:51-08:00","id":1356520,"title":"","content":"Does it have to be exactly like the Hulk? I only ask because Hulk, Doctor Solar, Captain Atom, Firestorm, and Doctor Manhattan are all essentially different takes on the same basic concept. There are also some rather fascinating alternate takes and pastiches in What If and Planetary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T14:57:11-08:00","id":1356537,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thinking things through further, the Transformation power wouldn't let me bypass the Quantum limit on Mega-Stats. It also doesn't allow you to take physical Mega-Edges, despite letting you take the Body Modification, Durability, and sensory Mega-Edges. I'm ignoring that bit and letting Dr. Banner take physical Mega-Edges via Transformation. Here is Dr. Bruce Banner as a (mostly) legal starting character:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Attributes-</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Might: 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dexterity: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intellect: 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cunning: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resolve: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence: 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manipulation: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Composure: 4</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Paths-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Origin Path: Suburbia</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Role Path: Technology Expert</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Society Path: Freelance Nova (adapted from Freelance Psion)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Skills-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Close Combat: 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Enigmas: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Humanities: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Larceny: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Medicine: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Pilot: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Science: 5 (Specialty: Radiation)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Survival: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Technology: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Skill Trick: R&amp;D Expert</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Edges-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fame or Alternate Identity (from being a Nova)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Big Hearted</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Patron (1)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Lightning Calculator</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Covert (1)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Danger Sense</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Quantum: 4 (48 xp)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Transformation: 5, -2 tag (only turns into the Hulk), -1 tag (only when angry), +1 tag (Attribute swap), +2 tag (Duration), +3 tag (Extra Traits). (96 xp)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">6 xp left over</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hulk-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Attributes-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Might: 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dexterity: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina: 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intellect: 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cunning: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resolve: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence: 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manipulation: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Composure: 4</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mega-Might: 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mega-Crush (1), Mega-Lifting (1), Quantum Leap (1), Shockwave (1), Thunderclap (1)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mega-Dexterity: 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mega-Stamina: 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dense Flesh (2), Regeneration (1)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Durability: 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Detection (astral beings): 1 [taken despite lacking Mega-Cunning, as per the Transformation power's text allowing you to take sensory Mega-Edges without letting you take Mega-Cunning]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">With more xp, go for Quantum +1, Mega-Might +1, Mega-Stamina +2, Durability +2, Mega-Speed (1), Rapid Strike (1), Immunity (1), and Dense Flesh +3. Dr. Banner could eventually get Mega-Intellect and related crafting Mega-Edges.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T17:24:38-08:00","id":1356559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition?p=1356485#post1356485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question before even try, but, how much experience is allowed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t have the Beta for 2nd Edition yet, but I assume there is a starting level of Experience? (One of the reasons for this post is my great curiosity for how the systems handle Character Creation differently.)<br /> <br /> If using 1st Edition, 30 Nova Points. (Though if you wanted to do a \u201cfully realized\u201d Hulk in 1st Ed, I\u2019d love to see how many Experience you could use to achieve that.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition?p=1356520#post1356520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it have to be exactly like the Hulk?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m personally very happy if it follows the \u201cDr. Jekyll &amp; Mr. Hyde\u201d core concept of most versions of the Hulk, but I am intrigued by other possibilities you are considering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition?p=1356520#post1356520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only ask because Hulk, Doctor Solar, Captain Atom, Firestorm, and Doctor Manhattan are all essentially different takes on the same basic concept. There are also some rather fascinating alternate takes and pastiches in What If and Planetary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see any of these characters/versions stated up for either Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T18:12:15-08:00","id":1356563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition?p=1356559#post1356559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t have the Beta for 2nd Edition yet, but I assume there is a starting level of Experience? (One of the reasons for this post is my great curiosity for how the systems handle Character Creation differently.)<br /> <br /> If using 1st Edition, 30 Nova Points. (Though if you wanted to do a \u201cfully realized\u201d Hulk in 1st Ed, I\u2019d love to see how many Experience you could use to achieve that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>2E starts with the Trinity core rules, but ignores the normal Step 5 and Step 6. You instead gain the Nova Template: Tier 3, Quantum 1, Fame or Alternate Identity Edge, 1 dot in a single Favored Approach Attribute (which seems to be ignored by the quick start character examples), and 150 xp, with power caps as set by the Storyteller. Alternate creation rules involve being given more or less starting xp, ranging from 75 through 300.<br /> <br /> Overall, the Transformation route I used for the Hulk makes the Power seem too strong. Why would anyone take either Growth or Shrinking when Transformation gives you both, and a bunch of other great options as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}